{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/165168-story-powers-and-serialized-chronicle-running","id":165168,"title":"Story-powers and \"serialized\" chronicle running","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-10T14:31:18-07:00","id":165168,"title":"Story-powers and \"serialized\" chronicle running","content":"This question could be posted at general <b>World of Darkness</b> forum, but only Werewolf as gameline use &quot;once per story&quot; archaic mechanics. And here I have problem. I run my games as TV series - I start with given date, like my now Werewolf game started on 1st January of 2014 in game world. And then I run chronicle chronologically, with multiple motives nd story arc working simultaneously. Think on structure of &quot;Game of Throne&quot; or &quot;True Blood&quot; series. I make. from time to time jump backward or forward in time, but that means most often that there is something important going on - or totally unimportant. I moved time when mage players were infiltrating by one month corporation headquater. And moved by three days in now game of Werewolf, when PCs were writing for they mentor to meet with them. <br /> <br /> Problem I have, with &quot;story based powers&quot; I an decide when to mark &quot;new story&quot;. Most of the time I create material for next game session and players are solving two, three subplots at once, each one could be treated as story. So when I don't have visible opening and closing of story - until you go to Chronicle Arc - what to do with powers talking about being used only once of story.<br /> <br /> Have anyone of you meet the same problem? How to solve it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T05:25:07-07:00","id":165823,"title":"","content":"Make it &quot;Once per X Sessions&quot;?<br /> <br /> If you're using Aspirations, let the power refresh upon completing their Long-term Goal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T05:57:06-07:00","id":165844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/165168-story-powers-and-serialized-chronicle-running?p=165823#post165823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Make it &quot;Once per X Sessions&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Different plots resolve at different peace, with one another interwoven with the previous. Like, character make territory for themselves, but in the meantime show ups the werebear summoned by awakening of they bear totem. And in between there is &quot;major plot&quot; of chronicle. Each one of them are run at the same time, one end quicker, second takes longer. When is there &quot;story&quot; moment for things like Cahalith Visions? When I can told player &quot;you can use this once more&quot;. And Totem grants Willpower per story - when would it be?<br /> <br /> This is why I hate &quot;per story&quot; powers - chronicles/campaigns are run organically, not artificially.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/165168-story-powers-and-serialized-chronicle-running?p=165823#post165823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're using Aspirations, let the power refresh upon completing their Long-term Goal?</div> </div> </div> </div>For one character it could be 1-2 sessions, for another it could 7-8. And if with beats itself it don't make real difference - you get Beats if you complete or just strife to Goal - when complete you just take another Aspiration. But there is a difference if completing one rest your Auspices powers in sessions, and other in 8 game sessions.<br /> <br /> But maybe it won't be this bad - devs says most powers will be per chapter (game session) kind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We\u2019ve beefed up many of the Auspice abilities, turning them into once-per-chapter abilities that evoke the werewolf\u2019s moon-given role. The Elodoth\u2019s ability, for example can either cause or end <i>kuruth</i> \u2014 but since she can only use it once per chapter she\u2019d better be very sure that she can deal with the consequences. </div> </div> </div>None the less, I have a problem with Willpower pool Totem grants to pack per story... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-11-2014, 09:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T07:56:50-07:00","id":165911,"title":"","content":"For the Totem Willpower/Essence thingy, just allow them per Chapter (Session). That works for us pretty well (we do not have a preponderance of either Willpower or Essence granted by the Totem, though, so your mileage may vary). Same goes for Aspect abilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T10:00:36-07:00","id":166062,"title":"","content":"Generally speaking, when the need arises to convert powers from narrative to chronological timers I find chapter = day, story = week, and chronicle = month to be a decent shorthand, borrowing from Demon's temporary glitch duration chart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T11:13:15-07:00","id":166107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/165168-story-powers-and-serialized-chronicle-running?p=166062#post166062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Generally speaking, when the need arises to convert powers from narrative to chronological timers I find chapter = day, story = week, and chronicle = month to be a decent shorthand, borrowing from Demon's temporary glitch duration chart.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like short hand, but too me, chronicle should be &quot;X years&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}